        "student_prefix_sha256": "d8b9de964587ea0bbd7b6beb1c17c191557e78c905b192f5defec339924d2b4c",
        "target": "Given:\n- Ann's speed: 6 miles per hour\n- Glenda's speed: 8 miles per hour\n- Time: 3 hours\n\nTo find the distance between them after 3 hours, we calculate the distance each person skates and then add those distances together.\n\nAnn's distance:\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 6 \\, \\text{miles/hour} \\times 3 \\, \\text{hours} = 18 \\, \\text{miles} \\]\n\nGlenda's distance:\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 8 \\, \\text{miles/hour} \\times 3 \\, \\text{hours} = 24 \\, \\text{miles} \\]\n\nTotal distance apart:\n\\[ 18 \\, \\text{miles} + 24 \\, \\text{miles} = 42 \\, \\text{miles} \\]\n\nFINAL: 42",
