fe","reason":"Forty minutes is 2/3 hour. Dustin reads 75×2/3 = 50 pages and Sam reads 24×2/3 = 16 pages, so the difference is 50 − 16 = 34.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5650"},{"independent_answer":"180","question_sha256":"38699f90d68e2e7a9860b4fcd1349c4000e7f84c64d252c76c040a0426cb8307","reason":"The segment times are 3/150 = 1/50 hour, 2/200 = 1/100 hour, and 1/300 hour. Their sum is 1/30 hour, so average speed is 6÷(1/30) = 180 km/h.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1722"},{"independent_answer":"42","question_sha256":"588604a2e27bd5fbce2cb18241e734c05b90dd5ae934a5314280fdcdee17f14d","reason":"Ann travels 6×3 = 18 miles and Glenda travels 8×3 = 24 miles. Because they move in opposite directions, their separation is 18 + 24 = 42 miles.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5462"}],"reviews":[{"checkable_expectation":true,"evidence_spans":["35 * 2 = 70 coins","I added 50 - 15 = 35 coins to my total."],"first_person":true,"full_text_read":true,"grounded_operations":null,"key":"gsm8k-train-59:rich","neutral_prefix_compatible":null,"no_padding":true,"prefix_reason":"The target's self-described calculations are visible, but it turns the prefix's ambiguous “collected 35 coins” over two hours into “35 coins each hour.” Whether that claim is supported cannot be resolved from the neutral prefix alone.","raw_call_sha256":"077b91b1b66e9a3f347000af90d4f6371c97677aaeae0526cf97236e536713fb","reason":"The response gives a substantive first-person calculation, concrete intermediates, and relevant operations. Its 120 result is correct only under the unresolved interpretation that 35 coins were collected in each of the two hours.","reusable_content":true,"status":"UNRESOLVED","student_prefix_sha256":"7c0945b5d66ce49c5673ec904c29cbffeadd955471baccfb1d33e029fb63f87e","target_sha256":"e706b255eeb4d1338ae907b73a7459c9d996ee9faa71abdbe7a340bf6f7a394e"},{"checkable_expectation":true,"evidence_spans":["15 (first hour) + 35 (second hour) + 35 (third hour) = 85 coins."